<title>USA: Right Start president resigns.</title>
<headline>Right Start president resigns.</headline>
<dateline>WESTLAKE VILLAGE, Calif. 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Right Start Inc Thursday said Stanley Fridstein has resigned as president and as a director of the company.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said no successor was named for Fridstein and that Jerry Welch, Chairman and Chief Executive Officer, would assume Mr. Fridstein's duties.</p>
<p>&quot;It's time to hand the baton over to the talented management team we've assembled at The Right Start,&quot; Fridstein said. &quot;I've thoroughly enjoyed building the company, however, it is time to pursue other interests that have been pulling at me for some time now.&quot;</p>
<p>The Right Start provides unique products for infants and young children up to age four.</p>
